# Build-context exclusions.
#
# The credential entries below are the load-bearing ones: they are the mechanism
# behind "no credentials baked into the image". A key that never enters the
# build context cannot be copied into a layer by a future `COPY . .`, and cannot
# be recovered from a pushed image by anyone who pulls it. Keep these in sync
# with the credential block in `.gitignore` — the two files defend the same
# property against two different accidents.
.env
.env.local
*-key.json
service-account*.json
application_default_credentials.json
*.pem
*.p12

# Version control and local tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info
build
dist

# Emulator and run scratch. `out/` holds the local JSONL event log; shipping a
# developer's local log into a production image would put fixture events into
# the deployed record.
out
.firestore-emulator
firebase-debug.log
*.log

# Not needed at runtime; they only make the image bigger and the build slower.
docs
tests
.DS_Store
